        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Length. \"Blind Man's Buff\" and \"Judgment of Paris\". Natural cotton tabby ground, printed with copperplates in blue. Two scenes alternate vertically, each occupying full width of cloth. One shows four girls playing blind man's buff; the other shows a shepherd, seated at left and three standing women in classical costume. Both selvedges present. Narrow band sen along top. Edges faded and browned."@en ;
